WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.41
This is journey twenty of Hewn, the software factory: sign in and sign out.

00:00:06.41 --> 00:00:08.17
Mission Control is private.

00:00:08.17 --> 00:00:11.64
Only GitHub accounts on Hewn's allow list may see it,

00:00:11.64 --> 00:00:16.62
a session lasts at most eight hours, and signing out has to end it for good.

00:00:16.62 --> 00:00:21.39
This video walks through how it was built: sign-in with GitHub, sign-out,

00:00:21.39 --> 00:00:25.78
the pages the API now serves with their protections, and the tests.

00:00:26.93 --> 00:00:32.07
Signed out, any page goes to sign-in, and after GitHub, back to that page.

00:00:32.07 --> 00:00:37.90
An account not on the allow list is refused with "This account doesn't have access".

00:00:37.90 --> 00:00:43.46
A session ends after eight hours or on sign-out, even if its cookie is replayed.

00:00:43.46 --> 00:00:48.94
And every page carries a content security policy that allows no inline scripts.

00:00:50.09 --> 00:00:51.77
Here is the sign-in flow.

00:00:51.77 --> 00:00:55.65
The API sends the browser to GitHub with a one-time state,

00:00:55.65 --> 00:00:58.53
kept in a protected cookie for ten minutes.

00:00:58.53 --> 00:01:02.82
When GitHub sends the user back, the callback checks that state,

00:01:02.82 --> 00:01:07.38
exchanges the code for the GitHub login, with a thirty second limit,

00:01:07.38 --> 00:01:10.13
and looks the login up in the allow list.

00:01:10.48 --> 00:01:13.70
The callback answers every outcome with a page.

00:01:13.70 --> 00:01:19.13
A forged state or a GitHub failure goes to sign-in saying GitHub didn't answer.

00:01:19.13 --> 00:01:24.07
A login not on the list goes to sign-in with that login, and no session.

00:01:24.07 --> 00:01:29.70
Otherwise the user gets an eight hour cookie, HTTP only, secure and same-site lax,

00:01:29.70 --> 00:01:34.09
and returns where they started, but only to a page on this site.

00:01:34.44 --> 00:01:39.29
The sign-in page reads its state from the address: denied, GitHub failed,

00:01:39.29 --> 00:01:41.62
the session expired, or signed out.

00:01:41.62 --> 00:01:43.68
Each is a state from the mocks.

00:01:44.83 --> 00:01:49.89
The mocks had no way to sign out, so the control was designed first in Magic

00:01:49.89 --> 00:01:53.82
Patterns: a Sign out icon button beside the signed-in user,

00:01:53.82 --> 00:01:55.61
at the foot of the sidebar.

00:01:55.61 --> 00:01:59.14
The mocks and the design system were rebuilt from it.

00:01:59.49 --> 00:02:05.43
Signing out records the session's id as revoked, and every request checks that id,

00:02:05.43 --> 00:02:09.34
held in memory so the check costs nothing per request.

00:02:09.34 --> 00:02:11.88
A replayed cookie gets four oh one.

00:02:11.88 --> 00:02:14.55
That is recorded as A D R twenty two.

00:02:14.90 --> 00:02:18.42
When any request gets four oh one while the app is open,

00:02:18.42 --> 00:02:22.76
because the eight hours passed or the user signed out in another tab,

00:02:22.76 --> 00:02:26.09
the app reloads at sign-in, saying the session ended,

00:02:26.09 --> 00:02:28.47
and comes back to the same page after.

00:02:29.62 --> 00:02:33.88
Until now only the development server served Mission Control.

00:02:33.88 --> 00:02:36.18
Now the API serves the built app.

00:02:36.18 --> 00:02:40.64
Signed out, a page redirects to sign-in with where it was going.

00:02:40.64 --> 00:02:46.43
Every response is marked no sniff, and every page gets the content security policy.

00:02:46.78 --> 00:02:51.31
Angular's build loads its stylesheet with one small inline handler,

00:02:51.31 --> 00:02:56.86
so the policy allows exactly that handler by its hash, and no other inline script.

00:02:56.86 --> 00:03:00.10
Frames are allowed only from the preview origin,

00:03:00.10 --> 00:03:03.15
and only this site may frame Mission Control.

00:03:03.50 --> 00:03:06.10
Here is what the API answers, signed out.

00:03:07.25 --> 00:03:10.88
The backend tests came first, and failed: six of them,

00:03:10.88 --> 00:03:14.11
with four oh one and a replayed cookie accepted.

00:03:14.11 --> 00:03:19.55
Now thirteen cover sign-in, refusal, a forged state, cancelling, the eight hours,

00:03:19.55 --> 00:03:23.65
sign-out with a replayed cookie, the pages and their headers.

00:03:24.00 --> 00:03:29.61
End to end, a test signs in through a fake GitHub authorize page and lands back on

00:03:29.61 --> 00:03:31.32
the page it started from.

00:03:31.67 --> 00:03:37.39
All green, the backend has two hundred and sixty one tests and the frontend four new

00:03:37.39 --> 00:03:38.14
view tests.

00:03:38.14 --> 00:03:42.23
End to end, there are eighteen new tests: six for behaviour,

00:03:42.23 --> 00:03:46.86
six visual comparisons with the mocks, and six accessibility checks.

00:03:48.01 --> 00:03:51.14
Here is Mission Control served by the API.

00:03:51.14 --> 00:03:53.82
Signed out, Workers goes to sign-in.

00:03:53.82 --> 00:04:00.08
Continue with GitHub opens GitHub's authorize page, here the fake one, and after it,

00:04:00.08 --> 00:04:01.13
Workers again.

00:04:01.13 --> 00:04:04.03
Sign out returns to sign-in, saying so.

00:04:04.38 --> 00:04:08.41
A login not on the allow list is refused, and told who to ask.

00:04:08.76 --> 00:04:12.60
GitHub failing, and a session that ended, each say what happened.

00:04:12.95 --> 00:04:16.22
The page reads the same in dark mode, and on a phone.

00:04:17.37 --> 00:04:19.28
Journey twenty is complete.

00:04:19.28 --> 00:04:24.22
Mission Control signs in with GitHub, and only the allow list gets in.

00:04:24.22 --> 00:04:29.24
Sessions end at eight hours or on sign-out, even for a replayed cookie.

00:04:29.24 --> 00:04:34.04
And the API serves every page with a strict content security policy.

00:04:34.04 --> 00:04:36.16
Next comes journey twenty one.
